      "id": "calculation-methods/2/2",
      "guide": "calculation-methods",
      "step": "2",
      "field": "body",
      "text": "The server computes it per station: target minus working VWC gives a deficit, the deficit becomes an amount of water, today’s ET adjusted by the crop coefficient is added, the daily maximum caps the total, and the result is divided by the Lynx reference amount.",
      "type": "calculation",
      "status": "Verified",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "intellidash",
          "ref": "production",
          "sha": "1aa4f28622cc3cc9637f0d61a438bf16bcf01924",
          "path": "api/Services/SpatialAdjustService.cs",
          "line": "2931-2932"
        },
        {
          "source": "intellidash",
          "ref": "production",
          "sha": "1aa4f28622cc3cc9637f0d61a438bf16bcf01924",
          "path": "api/Services/SpatialAdjustService.cs",
          "line": "2973-2974"
        },
        {
          "source": "intellidash",
          "ref": "production",
          "sha": "1aa4f28622cc3cc9637f0d61a438bf16bcf01924",
          "path": "api/Services/SpatialAdjustService.cs",
          "line": "3004-3015"
        },
        {
          "source": "intellidash",
          "ref": "production",
          "sha": "1aa4f28622cc3cc9637f0d61a438bf16bcf01924",
          "path": "api/Services/SpatialAdjustService.cs",
          "line": "3031-3043"
        },
        {
          "source": "doc",
          "ref": "docs/claims/calculations.md §2.2 The chain, per station, per day"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The working VWC is today's measured average, or the model's earlier prediction when there is no scan today (SpatialAdjustService.cs:3031-3032). Three steps the sentence leaves out: the deficit in VWC points is added to the ET in millimetres one for one, with no conversion; the sum is floored at 0 and multiplied by the station's soil factor before the cap (:3036-3039); and the result is rounded to a whole percentage (:3043). Whether one VWC point should equal one millimetre is listed for the experts in docs/claims/calculations.md §12.",
      "question": "",
      "developNote": "",
      "correction": ""
    },
